{{ display_name }} is a Python project with an explicit engineering policy and one verification workflow.

## Quickstart

```sh
uv sync --group ai-python-kit
just check
```

`just check` delegates to the kit recipe:

```sh
just --justfile .ai-python/kit/justfile --working-directory . check
```

The default run is offline and deterministic. Use `check online` to add live dependency vulnerability data.

{% if profile_cli %}
Run the command:

```sh
uv run {{ distribution_name }} World
```
{% endif %}

## Policy and ownership

- `.ai-python/policy.toml` is project-owned engineering policy.
- `.ai-python/config/` is project-owned native tool configuration.
- `.ai-python/kit/` is kit-managed and changes through reviewed Copier updates.
- `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `.python-version`, source, tests, root instructions, and CI are project-owned.
- `.copier-answers.ai-python-kit.yml` records template lineage and original scaffold answers.

Read `.ai-python/kit/references/engineering-policy.md` for the policy map and `.ai-python/kit/references/evidence.md` for verification evidence.

